Cleaning and surface properties — Mauro Taborelli (@cm-cleaning-source: 0, is #reference, #part-of @cm-sources) { r_1RDARBEFXDAW9Y2DNTJ2QBEP2E
Mauro Taborelli. *Cleaning and Surface Properties*, contribution to the CERN Accelerator School held in Glumslöv, Sweden, 6–16 June 2017. [arXiv:2006.01585v1, submitted 2 June 2020](https://arxiv.org/abs/2006.01585v1) · [19-page manuscript](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2006.01585v1). The author identifies it as an updated, shortened version of the earlier accelerator-vacuum school chapter.

Read the entire chapter: cleaning mechanisms, cleanliness assessment, process evaluation, packaging and functional surface properties. Use its UHV examples with their actual materials and equipment. Historical exposure limits, commercial availability statements and process recipes do not establish present requirements for another facility.

Sections 1–3.5 and selected later context were inspected on 30 October 2026; page 4 was viewed visually. Its supercritical-fluid prose says triple point where its diagram identifies the critical point. The phase lesson resolves that distinction. The experiments and all figures were not reproduced. The archive carries a non-exclusive distribution licence rather than a general reader adaptation licence. Keep the chapter and credited components external.

